# Marketplace award integrity (nihas V1.0.51).
# 1. award_market_bid: awarding a Marketplace bid closes every pending direct_quotes row on the indent
#    (both bidder branches). Writes no new rows.
# 2. tg_network_pool_commit_on_quote_accept: when a pool commit becomes exhausted, its other pending
#    direct_quotes (any indent) are set to rejected, so they stop showing as live offers.
# 3. notify_indent_supplier_requested: a Marketplace award emits 'awarded' (not 'Quote requested');
#    a network quote award emits nothing here (lifecycle trigger already emits 'awarded');
#    the title/payload use indent_code, the label the Load Center card shows.
# Function bodies start from the live prod definitions; the only changes are the marked additions.
# direct_quotes.status has no 'superseded' value, so closed rows are 'rejected'.
#
# Not in this set: scripts/fix-marketplace-stale-quotes-backfill.sql (one-time data cleanup, run separately
# after review; prod needs the owner's GO).
#
# Apply only via: npm run db:push-set -- marketplace-award-integrity   (dry-run first; prod apply needs Vasanth's GO)
# Never via plain `supabase db push` / `npm run db:push`.
#
# Verify before applying:
#   npx jest supabase/migrations/__tests__/marketplaceAwardIntegrityReleaseSet.test.ts
# sha256 671d3b4c6eb1ea3a3f351be9f017b8ba92f857591ecf742cb6b7232c90f26cd0  20271118213000_marketplace_award_state_integrity.sql
